exports[`generated docs stay in sync with the contracts snapshots: llms.txt and system.md 1`] = `
"# Antoine Duvauchelle — Product Engineer

> I build design systems, polished UI, and the guardrails that let teams — and agents — ship them.

Ten years shipping production frontends, from startup studios to the booking funnel of Rail Europe. I care about the last 10% — interaction details, accessibility, perceived speed — and about making the right path the easy one for whoever builds next.

Before code, I was a journalist. I still write docs as if someone is actually going to read them.

## Case studies

- [Modernising a ten-year-old booking platform, one layer at a time](https://www.toyn.dev/work/rail-europe-migration/): Instead of a rewrite, a revamp — a legacy Rails monolith moved toward modern Rails and Hotwire, the mobile apps brought onto the same codebase, and booking pages made to feel faster.
- [A SvelteKit rebuild, stopped at 80% — and the team I helped hold together](https://www.toyn.dev/work/rail-europe-sveltekit/): First in-house engineer on a from-scratch rebuild of the B2C booking site, alongside a team of consultants. Developer, Scrum Master and facilitator — and, for months, a bit of the missing roles too.
- [dadama — an AI-built data-journalism engine, with guardrails](https://www.toyn.dev/work/dadama/): A framework-free static site generator for data stories, built with Claude Code in a few days. The interesting part isn't the speed — it's the frame that kept the agent honest.
- [Designing and building a calmer mental-health app](https://www.toyn.dev/work/holivia/): The whole frontend of a mental-health platform, designed and rebuilt — including a calming audio player and video calls with therapists, in vanilla JavaScript, CSS and HTML.

## Design system

- [Design system](https://www.toyn.dev/system/): tokens, contrast checks and component contracts, generated from the code.
- [Design system as Markdown](https://www.toyn.dev/system.md): the same tokens and contracts, for agents. Follow it when changing the site.

## Optional

- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/in/antoine-duvauchelle-333184433/)
- [Codeberg](https://codeberg.org/toyn)
- [GitHub](https://github.com/aduvau)
"
`;

exports[`generated docs stay in sync with the contracts snapshots: llms.txt and system.md 2`] = `
"# Antoine Duvauchelle — design system

Generated from \`styles/tokens.css\` and \`src/system/contracts.ts\`; don't edit by hand.
Rules for anyone changing the site, human or agent:

- Colours, px values and durations come from the tokens below; a test fails on any raw one elsewhere.
- Use the spacing, type and radius tokens too wherever one fits.
- Every CSS class belongs to exactly one contract. Add or update the contract first.
- Keep every contrast pair at or above its minimum, in both themes.

## Tokens

### color

| Token | Light | Dark |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`--color-bg\` | \`oklch(98.5% 0.006 85)\` | \`oklch(18% 0.008 70)\` |
| \`--color-surface\` | \`oklch(96% 0.008 85)\` | \`oklch(22% 0.01 70)\` |
| \`--color-fg\` | \`oklch(22% 0.01 70)\` | \`oklch(93% 0.008 85)\` |
| \`--color-muted\` | \`oklch(46% 0.012 70)\` | \`oklch(72% 0.01 80)\` |
| \`--color-border\` | \`oklch(88% 0.01 80)\` | \`oklch(32% 0.01 70)\` |
| \`--color-accent\` | \`oklch(48% 0.16 262)\` | \`oklch(76% 0.12 262)\` |
| \`--color-accent-fg\` | \`oklch(98.5% 0.006 85)\` | \`oklch(18% 0.008 70)\` |
| \`--color-focus\` | \`oklch(55% 0.2 262)\` | \`oklch(78% 0.14 262)\` |

### font

| Token | Value |
| --- | --- |
| \`--font-sans\` | \`system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif\` |
| \`--font-mono\` | \`ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace\` |

### text

| Token | Value |
| --- | --- |
| \`--text-sm\` | \`0.875rem\` |
| \`--text-base\` | \`1.0625rem\` |
| \`--text-lg\` | \`clamp(1.1875rem, 1.1rem + 0.4vw, 1.375rem)\` |
| \`--text-xl\` | \`clamp(1.5rem, 1.3rem + 0.9vw, 2rem)\` |
| \`--text-2xl\` | \`clamp(2rem, 1.6rem + 2vw, 3.25rem)\` |

### leading

