## Contrast pairs

| Text / UI | On | Minimum | Light | Dark | Used for |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| \`--color-accent\` | \`--color-bg\` | 4.50:1 | 6.44:1 | 8.71:1 | Link: link text |
| \`--color-focus\` | \`--color-bg\` | 3.00:1 | 4.83:1 | 9.11:1 | Link: focus ring |
| \`--color-focus\` | \`--color-surface\` | 3.00:1 | 4.48:1 | 8.39:1 | Link: focus ring on surfaces |
| \`--color-bg\` | \`--color-fg\` | 4.50:1 | 16.60:1 | 15.31:1 | Button: label on the inverted pill |
| \`--color-fg\` | \`--color-surface\` | 4.50:1 | 15.43:1 | 14.10:1 | Card: title and summary; Design system page: examples |
| \`--color-muted\` | \`--color-surface\` | 4.50:1 | 6.36:1 | 6.98:1 | Card: eyebrow and impact labels; Muted: secondary text on surfaces |
| \`--color-fg\` | \`--color-bg\` | 4.50:1 | 16.60:1 | 15.31:1 | Page: body text; Design system page: body text |
| \`--color-muted\` | \`--color-bg\` | 4.50:1 | 6.84:1 | 7.58:1 | Page: secondary text; Design system page: secondary text; Muted: secondary text |
| \`--color-accent\` | \`--color-surface\` | 4.50:1 | 5.98:1 | 8.02:1 | Design system page: links in examples |
| \`--color-accent-fg\` | \`--color-accent\` | 4.50:1 | 6.44:1 | 8.71:1 | Skip link: label |

## Contracts

### Link

*component.* Inline navigation, in text and lists. External links say so to screen readers.

**Selectors:** \`a\`

**States**

- default
- hover (underline moves down)
- focus-visible (focus ring)

**Accessibility**

- Underlined, so links don't rely on colour alone.
- External links get a visually hidden “(external)” and \`rel="noopener"\`.
- Every focusable element shows the global \`:focus-visible\` ring (\`--focus-width\`, \`--color-focus\`).

**Do**

- Use \`linkTo()\` for links built from content, so external links are labelled.

**Don't**

- Don't remove the underline or the focus ring.

### Button

*component.* The one primary call to action of a page. A link styled as a pill, inverted colours.

**Selectors:** \`.button\`

**States**

- default
- hover (lifts by \`--lift-sm\`)
- active
- focus-visible

**Accessibility**

- It is an \`<a>\`: it navigates, so it is a link, not a \`<button>\`.
- The lift is a transform on \`--duration-fast\`, which is 0 under reduced motion.

**Do**

- Keep one per page, for the main action.

**Don't**

- Don't use it for in-page actions that need a \`<button>\`.

### Card

*component.* A case study teaser in the “Selected work” grid: cover, eyebrow, title, summary, impact.

**Selectors:** \`.cards\` \`.card\` \`.card-cover\` \`.is-portrait\` \`.card-title\` \`.card-link\`

**States**

- default
- hover / focus-within (accent border, lifts, cover zooms)
- portrait cover

**Accessibility**

- One link per card, on the title; its \`::after\` stretches the hit area over the whole card.
- The focus ring is drawn around the card, through that \`::after\`.
- The cover keeps the alt text written in the content.

**Do**

- Wrap cards in \`.cards\` (a \`<ul>\`), one \`<li class="card">\` each.

**Don't**

- Don't add a second link inside a card: the stretched link would cover it.

### Eyebrow

*component.* A short uppercase label above a title: client and period, or “Next”.

**Selectors:** \`.eyebrow\`

**Accessibility**

- A plain paragraph, before the heading it introduces; uppercase is CSS only.

**Don't**

- Don't use it as a heading.

### Impact

*component.* Measured results of a case study: a big figure and what it measures.

**Selectors:** \`.impact\` \`.impact-item\`

**Accessibility**

- A \`<dl>\` labelled “Impact”: the label (\`dt\`) comes before the figure (\`dd\`) in the source, the figure is shown first with \`column-reverse\`.
- Figures use tabular numbers.

**Do**

- Only figures with a source: the resume, or a before/after measurement.

**Don't**

- Don't round or invent numbers to fill the row.

### Tags

*component.* The stack of a case study, as small outlined pills.

**Selectors:** \`.tags\` \`.tag\`

**Accessibility**

- A \`<ul>\` labelled “Stack”, so it is announced as a list.

**Don't**

- Don't make tags interactive: they are not filters.

### Screenshot

*component.* A WebP screenshot with an optional dark-mode variant and caption.

**Selectors:** \`.case-cover\` \`.shot\` \`.gallery\`

**States**

- light
- dark (swapped with \`prefers-color-scheme\` when a dark shot exists)

**Accessibility**

- Alt text is required by the content schema; the build fails without it.
- Width and height come from the file, so images don't shift the layout.
- Lazy-loaded, except the cover of a case study.

### Hero

*component.* The top of the home page: name and role (the \`h1\`), tagline, intro and the call to action.

**Selectors:** \`.hero\` \`.hero-name\` \`.hero-role\` \`.tagline\` \`.intro\`

**Accessibility**

- The \`h1\` holds the name and role; the tagline is a paragraph styled large.
- Only on the home page, since it holds the \`h1\`; the example shows the tagline and intro only.

### Practice

*component.* One way of working, in the “How I work” grid.

**Selectors:** \`.practices\` \`.practice\`

**Accessibility**

- Each practice is a list item with an \`h3\`, under the section's \`h2\`.

### Timeline

*component.* Experience by organisation, with its roles; then education.

**Selectors:** \`.timeline\` \`.timeline-item\` \`.timeline-org\` \`.timeline-period\` \`.timeline-role\` \`.timeline-role-title\` \`.education\`

**Accessibility**

- An ordered list, most recent first; each organisation is an \`h3\`.

### Prose

*component.* The Markdown body of a case study, at a readable line length.

**Selectors:** \`.prose\`

**Accessibility**

- Headings in the Markdown start at \`h2\`, under the case study's \`h1\`.

### Page

*layout.* Page frame: centred column, header, sections and the contact footer.

**Selectors:** \`.page\` \`.section\` \`.subheading\` \`.site-header\` \`.site-name\` \`.site-footer\` \`.contact-lead\` \`.contact-links\` \`.colophon\` \`body\` \`h1\` \`h2\` \`h3\` \`p\` \`ul\` \`ol\` \`img\` \`figcaption\` \`code\`

**Accessibility**

- One \`h1\` per page, headings never skip a level, \`<html lang="en">\`.
- Sections are labelled by their heading (\`aria-labelledby\`).
- Light and dark themes follow \`prefers-color-scheme\`; there is no toggle and no JavaScript.

### Case study

*layout.* The structure of a case study page: back link, header, cover, impact, prose, links, next.

**Selectors:** \`.case\` \`.back\` \`.case-header\` \`.case-links\` \`.next\`

**Accessibility**

- The “Next case study” block is a \`<nav>\` with its own label.

### Design system page

*layout.* This page: token swatches and scales, contrast table, and one entry per contract.

**Selectors:** \`.system-toc\` \`.swatches\` \`.swatch\` \`.swatch-chip\` \`.table-scroll\` \`.system-table\` \`.type-sample\` \`.space-bar\` \`.contract\` \`.contract-spec\` \`.contract-example\`

**Accessibility**

- Contrast ratios are computed at build time, in both themes, from \`tokens.css\`.
- Examples are rendered by the same functions as the real pages, with the real content.

### Skip link

*utility.* “Skip to content”, the first focusable element of every page; visible on focus only.

**Selectors:** \`.skip-link\`

**States**

- hidden
- focus-visible (slides in)

**Accessibility**

- Targets \`#main\`; every page has a \`<main id="main">\`. Press Tab at the top of any page to see it.

### Visually hidden

*utility.* Text for screen readers only, e.g. “(external)” after a link.

**Selectors:** \`.visually-hidden\`

**Accessibility**

- Hidden with \`clip-path\`, never \`display: none\`, so it is still read out.

### Muted

*utility.* Secondary text colour.

**Selectors:** \`.muted\`

**Accessibility**

- \`--color-muted\` passes AA on both backgrounds, in both themes.
"
`;
